{"records":[{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s3jtdhjdbs","title":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Protein import motor complex reacts to mitochondrial misfolding by reducing protein import and activating mitophagy'","description":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Mitochondrial import loss induces mitophagy without membrane depolarization'. We hypothesized that inhibition of mitochondrial protein import induced mitophagy independent of mitochondrial depolarization. This dataset contains raw Illumina sequencing data for all samples from a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen for mitophagy regulators. The genome-wide library is Brunello from Doench et al Nat Biotechnol. 2016. We found that the pre-sequence translocase-associated motor complex PAM controls mitophagy induction. Loss of PAM caused a loss in protein import and was sufficient to induce mitophagy without depolarization.\nThe samples have been sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 in single end mode with 75+8 cycles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-05T15:38:53.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s3jtdhjdbs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s3jtdhjdbs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Michaelis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Melinda","last_name":"Brunstein","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Süleyman","last_name":"Bozkurt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ludovico","last_name":"Alves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Wegner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manuel","last_name":"Kaulich","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Pohl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Münch","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Mitochondrion","Mitophagy","Genetic Screening","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vs9fwhbcvj","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC High","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_High to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:42.171Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vs9fwhbcvj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vs9fwhbcvj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"p5t6d78zn8","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC Low","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low  to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:58.456Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/p5t6d78zn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/p5t6d78zn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4r55hvz87r","title":"Negative DNA supercoiling induces genome-wide Cas9 off-target activity. Newton MD et al","description":"CRISPR/Cas9 is a powerful gene-editing technology, however off-target activity remains an important consideration for therapeutic applications. We have previous-ly shown that force stretching DNA induces off-target activity and hypothesised that distortions of the DNA topology in vivo, such as negative DNA supercoiling, could reduce Cas9 specificity. Using single-molecule optical-tweezers, we demonstrate that negative supercoiling λ-DNA induces sequence-specific Cas9 off-target bind-ing at multiple sites, even at low forces. Using an adapted CIRCLE-seq approach, we detect over 10,000 negative supercoiling induced Cas9 off-target double-strand breaks genome wide, caused by increased mismatch tolerance. We further demon-strate in vivo that directed local DNA distortion increases off-target activity in cells and that induced off-target events can be detected during Cas9 genome-editing. These data demonstrate that Cas9 off-target activity is regulated by DNA topology in vitro and in vivo, suggesting that cellular processes, such as transcription and replication, could induce off-target activity at previously overlooked sites. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-12T08:20:22.495Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4r55hvz87r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4r55hvz87r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Matt","last_name":"Newton","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology","Single Molecule Imaging","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Genome Editing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"5pfdty7zd6","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC  - Undifferentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in undifferentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples directly.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:32.252Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/5pfdty7zd6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/5pfdty7zd6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xvk2gk4hw3","title":"Data of Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","description":"Raw data for figures in Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-25T15:27:04.321Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xvk2gk4hw3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xvk2gk4hw3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qian","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Developmental Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"z4ht3txn2k","title":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023","description":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023. This dataset contains Source and additional Data for all figures.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-06T07:16:19.286Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/z4ht3txn2k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/z4ht3txn2k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Daniel","last_name":"Durocher","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yichao","last_name":"Zhao","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":null}],"categories":["DNA Replication","DNA Repair","Flow Cytometry","Cancer Chemotherapy","DNA Damage","Functional Genomics","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":125807,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":154,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":125807,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":125303,"restricted":62,"embargoed":442},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2130},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1466},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":583},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":446},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":428},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":396},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific